        <h1>LeetCode 856: Score of Parentheses (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Given a balanced parentheses string s, return the score of the string. The score of a
                balanced parentheses string is based on the following rules: "()" has a score of 1, AB has a
                score of A + B where A and B are balanced parentheses strings, and (A) has a score of 2 * A
                where A is a balanced parentheses string.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: s = "(()(()))"<br>
                Output: 6<br>
                Explanation: The outer pair doubles the score of its contents, which combine an inner "()"
                worth 1 and a nested "(())" worth 2, giving a total of 6.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int scoreOfParentheses(string str) {
        stack&lt;int&gt; scores;
        scores.push(0);

        for (char ch : str) {
            if (ch == '(') {
                scores.push(0);
            } else {
                int innerScore = scores.top();
                scores.pop();

                int outerScore = scores.top();
                scores.pop();

                scores.push(outerScore + max(2 * innerScore, 1));
            }
        }

        return scores.top();
    }
};</code></pre>
